  "note": "Annual election of three members of the Holywood Urban Council, January 1932; the retiring members were returned unopposed (Northern Herald, 16 January 1932, p. 6). The only new nomination, William Frank Parvin, was withdrawn. The three retiring members, Councillors Frank Hamilton, John Woods and Frederick Graham, were therefore automatically elected without a poll. Returned unopposed."
